nodecode-bluesky-feed is a rewrite of TakeshiTGAL's TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-author-feed:

  https://github.com/TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-author-feed
  commit d3c9497d3f62b7f49aa0fa6131a7cd30278d80a8
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the reading and the watch. The plugin's three tools
(`profile_get`, `author_feed`, `author_watch`) are `bluesky_profile`,
`bluesky_feed` and `bluesky_watch` here, and they send the same two reads to
the same public AppView, `app.bsky.actor.getProfile` and
`app.bsky.feed.getAuthorFeed`, with `limit=10` and `filter=posts_no_replies`,
no key and no `Authorization` header. The profile fields it kept and the
fields it dropped (avatar, banner, description, pinned post) are the same; a
repost still says so and keeps the original author; a pin is still not a new
post. The watch is the same design: one saved account, its post addresses
kept in one file, the first check a baseline that announces nothing, at most
three pages per check, and the possible-miss note when every row read was new
and the feed still offered more. The plugin's `hermes author-feed
schedule|unschedule|status` becomes `/bluesky watch|check|status|forget`, and
its interval, deliver-target and cron-job bookkeeping become the shipped
`cron` cell's.

What was left out, and why: the plugin started its watch from a generated
Python script that Hermes cron ran, and that script proved its own job id
against `cron/executions.db` and `cron/jobs.json` before it advanced what it
had seen. A cell runs inside Nodecode, which has a scheduler of its own, so
the script, the job-id proof, the `--no-agent --script` cron plumbing and the
delivery allowlist (Hermes platforms, `bot-chat`, `origin`/`local`/`all`)
stay with the plugin: `/bluesky watch HANDLE` saves the account and `cron`
runs `bluesky_watch` on whatever schedule the operator wants. The plugin's
state file keeps the same facts (DID, handle, seen post addresses, baseline
flag) but lives in one file under the Nodecode home rather than in the Hermes
plugin-data folder, and the split between "the saved cron job may advance
what was seen" and "a manual call may not" is gone: in a cell the watch verb
is the only thing that advances it.
